{
  "title": "Dua for the Eighth Hour",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "The eighth hour, which is the space of time between the amount of four units of prayer after the Noon Prayer and the Afternoon Prayer, is dedicated to Imam Ali ibn Musa al-Rida (a). The supplication at this hour is the following:\nيَا خَيْرَ مَدْعُوٍّ يَا خَيْرَ مَنْ اَعْطٰى يَا خَيْرَ مَنْ سُئِلَ يَا مَنْ اَضَاۤءَ بِاسْمِهِ ضَوْءُ النَّهَارِ وَ اَظْلَمَ بِهِ ظُلْمَةُ اللَّيْلِ وَ سَالَ بِاسْمِهِ وَابِلُ السَّيْلِ وَ رَزَقَ اَوْلِيَاۤئَهُ كُلَّ خَيْرٍ يَا مَنْ عَلَا السَّمٰوَاتِ نُوْرُهُ وَ الْاَرْضَ ضَوْئُهُ وَالشَّرْقَ وَالْغَرْبَ رَحْمَتُهُ يَا وَاسِعَ الْجُوْدِ اَسْئَلُكَ بِحَقِّ عَلِيِّ بْنِ مُوْسَى الرِّضَا عَلَيْهِمَا السَّلَامُ وَ اُقَدِّمُهُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْ حَوَاۤئِجِيْ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ اَنْ تَفْعَلَ بِيْ كَذَا وَ كَذَا۔\nYAA KHAYRA MAD-U'W, YAA KHAYRA MAN A'TAA, YAA KHAYRA MAN SU-IL, YAA MAN ADAAA-A BI-ISMIHI DAW-UN NAHAAR, WA AZLAMA BIHI ZULMATUL LAYL, WA SAALA BI-ISMIHI WAABILUS SAYL, WA RAZAQA AWLIYAAA-AHU KULLA KHAYR, YAA MAN A'LAS SAMAAWAATI NOORUHU WAL ARDA DAW-UHU WASH SHARQA WAL GHARBA RAHMATUH, YAA WAASI-A'L JOOD, AS-ALUKA BI-HAQQI A'LIYYIBNI MOOSAR RIDAA A'LAYHIMAS SALAAM, WA UQADDIMUHU BAYNA YADAY HAWAAA-IJEE, AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WA AN TAF-A'LA BEE KAZAA WA KAZAA.\nO Best of those called upon! O Best of those who give! O Best of those who are asked! O He by Whose name the light of day shines and the darkness of night falls, by Whose name the downpour of the flood streams, and Who has provided His intimate friends with every good! O He Whose light rises above the heavens, Whose radiance covers the earth, and Whose mercy spans east and west! O Vast in generosity! I beseech You by the right of Ali ibn Musa al-Rida, upon both of them be peace, and I present him before my needs, that You bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, and that You do for me such-and-such.\nYou may now mention your needs."
}
